1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:02,300
Meet ai and ay.

2
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:05,340
Two spellings, one sound.

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:07,520
They both say the same thing.

4
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:08,580
Ayyy!

5
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:09,900
Listen.

6
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:11,840
Rain.

7
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:13,400
Play.

8
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:16,360
Same sound, different spelling.

9
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,020
So how do you know which one to write?

10
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:21,020
Here's the secret.

11
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:25,220
It's all about WHERE the sound sits in the word.

12
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:29,720
Every word has a beginning, a middle, and an end.

13
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:33,750
When the sound is in the MIDDLE, we write ai.

14
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:35,320
Look.

15
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:36,680
R.

16
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:38,020
Ai.

17
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:39,420
N.

18
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,840
Rain!

19
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,760
There are letters before it, and letters after it.

20
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,580
It's tucked right in the middle.

21
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,570
But when the sound is at the very END, we write ay.

22
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:54,580
D.

23
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:56,280
Ay.

24
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:57,700
Day!

25
00:00:58,620 --> 00:00:59,820
Nothing comes after it.

26
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:01,980
That's why we use ay.

27
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:04,720
So we never write rayn.

28
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:07,600
And we never write dai.

29
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,200
Ai in the middle.

30
00:01:11,320 --> 00:01:12,440
Ay at the end.

31
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:14,340
Let's see it.

32
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:15,740
Rain.

33
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:17,820
Snail.

34
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:19,840
Train.

35
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:21,920
Paint.

36
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:24,140
Tail.

37
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:26,120
Chain.

38
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:29,260
Every one has ai in the middle.

39
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:31,300
Now the end ones.

40
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:33,060
Day.

41
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:35,000
Play.

42
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:37,140
Say.

43
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:39,460
Stay.

44
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:41,660
Tray.

45
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:43,560
Hay.

46
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,940
Every one finishes with ay.

47
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:49,080
Now it's your turn!

48
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:50,640
Here's the word.

49
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:51,880
Paint.

50
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,860
Is it ai, or ay?

51
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:57,640
It's ai!

52
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,940
Because the sound is in the middle.

53
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,600
So remember.

54
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:06,120
Ai hides in the middle, ay finishes the word.

55
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:10,140
Want to practice every phonics rule?

56
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:11,420
Get the English Learning app.

57
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:12,280
It's free!
